  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 223 PM EDT Wed Jul 29 2026\n\n- Dry Conditions Continue into Friday\n\nUpper level ridging will continue to build into the area into\nThursday. High pressure will be in place into Friday with dry\nconditions expected and highs in the 80s with lows in the 50s to\nlow 60s. Expect cooler daytime temperatures along the lakeshore \nwith winds off of Lake Michigan.\n\n- Rain Chances Increase Friday Night Into Saturday\n\nA shortwave trough moves through Friday night into Saturday\nbringing our next chance for rain. The surface low is expected to\ntrack south of the area, but increasing precipitable water values\nand mid level lift should support the development of rain showers\nstarting Friday night and continuing into Saturday. At this time\nCAPE is limited, but can't rule out some thunder during this\ntimeframe. Rain likely clears Saturday night, but some \nvariability in timing exists. If the trough lingers we could see \nrain chances extend into Saturday night. After the trough clears \npressure heights increase and high pressure builds back into the \narea.",
